                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Short version: 73%[/h1]\nRobot Legions Reborn is the updated, standalone version of an otherwise free Flash game of the same name. With an additional difficulty and an endless mode, it doesn’t offer too much more, but plenty enough to justify its nominal price for those who love top-down arcade shooters.\n\n[h1]Long version:[/h1]\nThe free Flash version of Robot Legions is a relatively popular title on those sites that specialise in similar games, so maybe it was natural to create a standalone, Flash-free version of it.\n\nBoth versions are top-down arcade twin-stick shooters of the kind where you can collect money to buy different kind of upgrades. These upgrades are quite important to pass some later levels; to the point where some players may need to grind earlier stages to get enough firepower and health to survive later ones.\nEven shooter veterans can find sufficient challenge, thanks to the new difficulty added to the Steam release: enemies are more aggressive and shoot shrapnel upon death, turning each stage into lightweight bullet hells.\n\nAlthough the game only offers 18 stages (and an optional arcade mode), it is hard to argue that it offers more than enough for its two-dollar price. So, if you want something smaller to scratch that top-down shooter itch, Robot Legions Reborn offers one of the best bangs for its buck.",
